<title>USA: HemoCleanse licenses Monsanto patents.</title>
<headline>HemoCleanse licenses Monsanto patents.</headline>
<dateline>WEST LAFAYETTE, Ind. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>HemoCleanse Inc said Thursday it acquired an exclusive license to key Monsanto Co patents for the development of a bio-artificial liver assist device.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not announced.</p>
<p>The company said the device pumps blood from the patient into a bioreactor containing pig liver cells that can clean toxins from the blood. The device is currently being tested at Washington University Hospital in St. Louis, HemoCleanse said.</p>
<p>HemoCleanse develops products that remove toxins and balance blood chemistry outside of the body.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
